From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:51:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: Detect a power-on reset of an SDZ
 group amp at resume

The previous change restores an SDZ group from a power-on reset when the
resume comes through firmware. A sleep can still cut the shared SDZ line
or the amps' supply without the firmware reporting it, for example an
s2idle resume after a deep sleep that failed half way. The amps then sit
in their reset state with the cache believing otherwise, and the first
stream latches an over-current on a woofer amp, which takes the whole
group down.

Ask the amp. PWR_CTRL resets to 0x1a with BOP_SRC clear, and the probe
sets BOP_SRC on every SN012776, so a read that bypasses the cache tells
a reset amp from one that kept its registers. When it was reset, or does
not answer, take the power-on path. This costs one register read per amp
per resume.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index 82a90810d9..c7e270376c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -432,6 +432,25 @@ static int tas2764_codec_suspend(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Whether the amp came back from a power-on reset, read from the amp itself:
+ * PWR_CTRL resets to 0x1a with BOP_SRC clear, and the probe sets BOP_SRC on
+ * every SN012776. A failed read counts as lost too. Bypasses the cache, which
+ * still holds the probe's value.
+ */
+static bool tas2764_lost_state(struct tas2764_priv *tas2764)
+{
+	unsigned int val;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (tas2764->devid != DEVID_SN012776)
+		return false;
+	regcache_cache_bypass(tas2764->regmap, true);
+	ret = regmap_read(tas2764->regmap, TAS2764_PWR_CTRL, &val);
+	regcache_cache_bypass(tas2764->regmap, false);
+	return ret || !(val & TAS2764_PWR_CTRL_BOP_SRC);
+}
+
 static int tas2764_codec_resume(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 {
 	struct tas2764_priv *tas2764 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
@@ -460,6 +479,17 @@ static int tas2764_codec_resume(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 
 	regcache_cache_only(tas2764->regmap, false);
 
+	/*
+	 * Any other sleep that cut the line or the supply (an s2idle wake
+	 * after a deep sleep that failed half way) leaves the same reset
+	 * state without the firmware saying so; a stream started on it
+	 * latches an over-current on a woofer amp. Check the amp itself.
+	 */
+	if (tas2764->sdz_group && !power_on && tas2764_lost_state(tas2764)) {
+		dev_warn(tas2764->dev, "registers lost in a sleep: restoring as from power-on\n");
+		power_on = true;
+	}
+
 	if (power_on) {
 		/* SDZ high to the first I2C access, as at probe */
 		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
-- 
